-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Attribution & design-inspiration notices
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

codeagent-minimal is an ORIGINAL implementation. Where functionality or
architecture is *inspired by* an open-source project, the inspiration is
acknowledged here for transparency. All inspired ideas were re-implemented
from scratch in pure Python standard library — no third-party source code is
copied, bundled, or linked into this repository, and no derivative-work
obligation is assumed beyond what Apache-2.0 itself already imposes on
downstream users.

The following projects / products inspired *design ideas only*
(self-implemented, not copied):

  * FSoft CodeWiki (MIT)
      - "Reuse-first" structured code-atom knowledge retrieval concept,
        re-implemented as the local code-atom reuse layer (atoms/ + reuse).
  * dep_audit / Semgrep-style data-flow taint analysis (Semgrep is LGPL)
      - The source->sink taint-analysis *idea*, re-implemented from scratch
        as a pure-stdlib static taint engine (dep_scan.py / dep-scan atom).
        No Semgrep or dep_audit source is used.
  * OpenCode (MIT)
      - MCP client / SKILL skills / CodeMode orchestration / fine-grained
        permission (allow / ask / deny) *concepts*, re-implemented from
        scratch (mcp-client, code-skill atoms; closed-source CodeMode lives
        outside this repository).
  * CodeReview / test-harness methodologies (variously MIT / Apache-2.0)
      - Static review dimensions and mutation / fuzz testing *approaches*,
        re-implemented as pure-stdlib modules (review.py, test_harness.py,
        fuzz_engine.py, reg_guard.py).

MIT is a permissive license compatible with Apache-2.0 for downstream use.
Because no MIT source was copied into this repository, no MIT notice
inclusion or derivative-work obligation is triggered for this project.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Dependency boundary
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

codeagent-minimal has ZERO third-party RUNTIME dependencies — it runs on the
Python standard library only (ast / re / json / subprocess / importlib ...).
Optional analyzers (bandit, pyflakes, coverage, pytest) are detected at
runtime and gracefully skipped when absent; they are development
conveniences, not required dependencies, and introduce no license obligation
for the shipped artifact.

-------------------------------------------------------------------------
Open-source kernel / closed-source orchestration boundary
-------------------------------------------------------------------------

The 16 atomic agents, the unified runtime (agent_runtime.py) and the unified
entry (codeagent.py) shipped in THIS repository are open source under
Apache-2.0. The closed-source assembler / orchestrator and CodeMode live in
the SEPARATE closed-source workspace and are NOT part of this repository and
are NOT shipped, linked, or required here.
